            <ArticleTitle>Hemoperitoneum secondary to avulsed short gastric arteries after vomiting: the first documented case in North America.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is the first documented case in North America wherein a 26-year-old man presented to the emergency room with hemoperitoneum secondary to avulsed short gastric arteries after violent emesis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
